# .mailmap — unify author identities for git log, git blame, and the
# GitHub contributors graph (https://github.com/dumixthestpd/sustech_survival/graphs/contributors).
#
# Format:  canonical-name <canonical-email>  <commit-name> <commit-email>
# If only email is provided, the most common name is used.
# If only name is provided, the most common email is used.
#
# Use the GitHub noreply form as canonical so the contributors graph
# links to the contributor's GitHub profile (noreply is auto-verified;
# the QQ email below is not, so without this mapping the QQ commit would
# appear as a ghost and the two commits would look like two different
# people).

# Xiao-La (PR #7) — Joyslog / xCipHanD fork: same person, two emails.
xiao-la <47178126+Xiao-La@users.noreply.github.com> Joyslog <47178126+Xiao-La@users.noreply.github.com>
xiao-la <47178126+Xiao-La@users.noreply.github.com> xiao-la <836772730@qq.com>